Reason:
These statements send the station AID (contained in `sta->aid`) to the firmware without any prior validation. When the AID exceeds 20, the firmware crashes, causing system instability. The driver did not check for an upper bound on the AID before passing it to firmware operations.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (sta->aid > MT7921_MAX_AID)
		return -ENOENT;
if (sta->aid > MT7921_MAX_AID)
		return -ENOENT;

Reason:
These added checks at the beginning of `mt7921_mac_sta_add` and `mt7921_mac_sta_event` reject any station with an AID greater than the firmware-defined maximum (MT7921_MAX_AID). By returning -ENOENT early, the driver avoids passing invalid AIDs to the firmware, thereby preventing the crash. This fix does not require changes to other parts of the driver since the invalid stations are simply not added or processed.

